/* Branch Chat page.

   Messages are encrypted in this file before they are sent. The server
   stores ciphertext. This page decrypts with the device key in IndexedDB.

   A deleted message stays in the thread as "Message removed". The text
   and file are gone on the server. Sync does not repeat old sequence
   numbers, so removals arrive on the gone cursor.

   An edit keeps the same seq. The browser encrypts the new text with the
   same message key and the server replaces the ciphertext. The edit
   cursor is how a client that already stored the row learns about it.
   The sender can edit their three newest live messages in that chat.
   An admin can edit any message this device can already open.

   Profile settings opens from the bottom-left picture, the username,
   or Profile settings in the menu. A click outside that popup closes it.
   Text size, color theme, and the profile picture stay in the hamburger menu.
   Each chat can keep its own background on this device. The server does not see it.

   The Android and Linux apps load this page. A refresh picks up message
   edits, authenticator setup, chat download, and password reset.
*/

