/* bv-char.js (new-snaps): the Beaver Builder delete animation (key "beaver"). Uses only shared helpers
   (snapTarget, snapReduced, fxWatch, woodWipe, woodCarry, playWoodSfx, bnColour, bnRand, $).
   The story: a beaver in a yellow hard hat hops in (thump, thump, thump with its tail), reaches up and grabs the
   message, which turns into a little log (with the message's colour in its rings). It chews the log down in a flurry
   of wood chips, turns round to its mud mound and builds a dam stick by stick (six clacks), pats it down with two tail
   slaps, then waddles off.
   How it is drawn:
   - The beaver and its dam are the stage's own SVG (BEAVER_SVG), so they stand where every character stands and mirror
     with the stage; their groups are re-posed every frame and the six sticks appear as they are placed.
   - The log and the wood chips are drawn on ONE fixed canvas over the chat (never mirrored), placed from on-screen
     positions of the beaver's mouth.
   - The message is a styled copy (woodCarry) for the grab, then becomes the log.
   - Everything is a function of time from one requestAnimationFrame loop, so every frame is a fresh in-between at any
     refresh rate. fxWatch thins the chips on a slow device; the beaver and the dam never lose detail.
   Timeline (ms from when it appears; matches beaver-sfx.mp3 thumps/chomps/clacks/slaps): see BV. The real message is
   hidden at BV.GRAB, well before the shared gap fold (3900-4600). Reduced motion: a plain wipe. */
